{"severity":"error","file":"errors/pure_violation_4.march","start_line":11,"start_col":4,"end_line":11,"end_col":21,"message":"`mod Pure` (declared `cap pure`) declares `needs IO.FileRead`, but a pure module cannot hold a capability: `needs` exists only to admit side effects, directly or through a stdlib wrapper such as `File.read` or `DateTime.now`.\n\nRemove the `needs` line, and move the code that needs it to a module without `cap pure`.","code":"pure_violation","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CONTRACT"}
